    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0056" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54Guat/pg26"/>

                <head>17. Telegram From the CIA
                        Station in [<hi rendition="#italic">place not declassified</hi>] to
                    the Central Intelligence Agency<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d17-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>[<hi rendition="#italic">place not declassified</hi>], <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1952-09-12T16:32:00+00:00">September 12, 1952,
                        1632Z</date>.</dateline>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">telegram indicator not declassified</hi>] 605. Ref:
                        DIR 18338.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d17-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Somoza advised Ambassador
                        Whelan that he and Trujillo have agreed on Guatemala and would take care of
                    situation. Venezuela apparently has agreed to cooperate. Details of Somoza–Trujillo agreement and plans not presently available. Source TNN
                    560 not yet <pb facs="0057" n="27" xml:id="pg27"/> advised of plans but will
                    furnish on receipt. Due to illness and preoccupation with other matters
                        Somoza has not yet briefed DYMAROON
                    on plans but has advised that he will do so. Advise if hqs desirous of receiving
                    information obtained from DYMAROON by cable.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
